{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLMqt1RjrnFT22edaPhx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is commit `e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e` in openmrs-core, titled \"TRUNK-6646: Env-var key normalization drops create_database_* / create_user_* credentials in scripted setup (#6145)\", by jwnasambu. The commit message names PR #6145.\n\n**The cause:** `normalizeEnvVariableKey` lowercases every environment variable name and turns `_` into `.`, except for keys in `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`. `CREATE_DATABASE_USERNAME`, `CREATE_DATABASE_PASSWORD`, `CREATE_USER_USERNAME` and `CREATE_USER_PASSWORD` were missing from that set. They became `create.database.username` and similar, so the lookup for `create_database_username` never matched and the wizard fell back to root with no password.\n\n**The fix:**\n- The commit adds those four keys to `NON_NORMALIZED_KEYS`, plus `CONNECTION_DRIVER_CLASS`, `IMPORT_TEST_DATA`, `REMOTE_URL`, `REMOTE_USERNAME`, `REMOTE_PASSWORD` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD_LOCKED`. The current file still has this list at lines 197–201.\n- It also changes how the installation script is read: `connection_driver_class` is accepted as a fallback, `import_test_data`/`add_demo_data` and the `remote_*` properties are read, and `admin.password.locked` is stored under its dotted name. Those edits are in the commit's diff but are not in the lines I read at HEAD.\n- The commit adds `InitializationFilterNormalizationTest.java` and two `InitializationFilterTest` cases covering these variables.\n\nI did not read the commit's diff in full, so the list above comes from the diff hunks plus the current file.\n\n**Lines that implement it at the current default branch:**\n- Whitelist: `web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java` lines 197–201.\n- Normalizer that uses the whitelist: same file, lines 1948–1953.\n- Where env vars are merged into the script properties: same file, lines 340–343.\n\nNothing in the repositories was modified. The search calls I made were `list_commits`, one `grep` for the ticket key, and `grep` for the normalizer symbols.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"repo\": \"openmrs-core\", \"commit\": \"e7052745fb78802c8adcd7c1962f3525e7050b1e\"},\n  {\"ticket\": \"TRUNK-6646\"},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 197, \"endLine\": 201},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 1948, \"endLine\": 1953},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/web/src/main/java/org/openmrs/web/filter/initialization/InitializationFilter.java\", \"startLine\": 340, \"endLine\": 343}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2270,"cache_read_input_tokens":21029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2270},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f96c9dd8-7448-43dd-96ae-9df02e48fe20","uuid":"a53c8aa5-debb-42c5-bc10-f14e8932b9c4","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:34:37.795Z","request_id":"req_011CgLMqsjJu7b9rseZoN3Da"}
